  "preamble": "Lenition of the voiceless bilabial stop [p] to the voiced bilabial fricative [β] combines voicing with spirantization while keeping the bilabial place. In Fijian, Proto-Oceanic *p became the bilabial fricative written ⟨v⟩ [β], so POc *pat 'four' is Fijian va and POc *pulan 'moon' is vula. Fijian distinguishes this bilabial [β] from labiodental [f].",
